  "contract": {
    "discovery": "GPU_CAP_TYPED_TILE_COMMANDS bit31, explicit persistent opcode-7 profile only. The default desktop profile and version-1 draw record stay unchanged.",
    "descriptor": "Magic 0x47545002 selects typed commands; the 64-word/256-byte descriptor layout and inner attachment descriptor version1 are unchanged. Magic 0x47545001 retains legacy 160-byte command records.",
    "records": "164 bytes: one exact type word (DRAW=0, CLEAR=1) followed by 40 payload words. Count includes every command. Full 33-bit allocation admission checks count*164, including exact 4GiB; no silent wrap.",
    "draw": "Payload is the complete prior inline draw record, including state and scissor words38/39.",
    "clear": "Payload0 packs minX,minY,maxX,maxY in five low bits per byte. Payload1/2 are color/depth masks, payload3/4 packed values, payload5..39 and high rectangle bits zero. Half-open tile-local rectangle; all active samples; empty/zero-mask valid no-ops.",
    "ownership": "One tagged FIFO with a union payload. Older geometry and OM work drain before clear offer; younger draw stays blocked until clear completion. End waits for command/FIFO/clear and render drain, then exports once.",
    "failure": "Unsupported/reserved encodings or invalid rectangles status1; clear LOAD memory fault status3. Cancel/reset drops unaccepted tokens but preserves offered/issued reads and accepted clear ownership. Reset discards its old completion.",
    "feedback": "Register failed clearDone before returning cancellation, avoiding a combinational cycle through the owner status. Clear valid is fenced on renderDrained so it does not close the draw gate on older accepted geometry/fan work."
  },
